    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d454">

                <pb facs="0637" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg547"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5860: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-21T19:00:00-05:00">February 21, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. Your 93, February 20, 11 a.m.—Hukuang loan.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>You are authorized to sign the joint memorandum.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Department would suggest, however, if your colleagues consent, that the
                        word “validity”, the seventh word from the end of the third paragraph of the
                        proposed joint memorandum, be changed to “value”, and that there be added to
                        the last paragraph of the proposed memorandum the words “and previous
                        memoranda and notes,” if in fact there were previous memoranda and notes on
                        the subject.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d454-f1"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d454-f1" n="2" xml:id="d454-f1-content">
                <p>The text of the joint memorandum, dated March 7, 1934, contained these changes,
                    except that the two words “and notes” were omitted (893.51/5876).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
